"kind":"trace",
"id":"square_blocks",
"source":"square_blocks.py",
"code":"import sys\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    d = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    v = list(map(int, d))\n    g = [v[0:3], v[3:6], v[6:9]]\n    t = []\n    for i in range(2):\n        x, y = g[i], g[i + 1]\n        row = []\n        for j in range(2):\n            a = x[j:j + 2]\n            b = y[j:j + 2]\n            row += [max(a + b)]\n        t += [row]\n    print(max(t[0] + t[1]))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n",
"alt":"A short version of the square table for a 3 by 3 grid. The nested loops fill a 2 by 2 table where each entry is the maximum of one 2 by 2 block of the grid. The last line takes the maximum of those four entries, which together cover the whole 3 by 3 square.",
